Subject: [PATCH 138/230] test(i18n): gate Persian text integrity on codepoint
 bug classes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

bel.1's garbled row ("لیگ برزیل پرو" — Persian copy holding Korean
characters) proves nobody ever machine-checks the FA strings, and a
human review pass cannot catch what a future data edit writes after
it. Two gates in the tracked suite, scanning string literals of
strings.ts, names.ts and server/messages.ts:

- Arabic ي (U+064A) / ك (U+0643) standing in for Persian ی/ک — the
  copy-paste-from-Arabic bug class that breaks search and shaping;
- any CJK character inside a string literal — no surface in this app
  is Korean/Japanese/Chinese, so any match is an accident;
- long untranslated Latin prose inside majority-Persian copy.

The reviewed names for sco.1 and bel.1 are pinned so renames are
deliberate. What still needs a native speaker: register/word-choice
review of the ~523 FA strings — documented in the report, not
assertable by code.

